exports[`git.pull.watch faults given: [case4] a watch record that will not parse when: [t0] a human reads the watches with get then: the unreadable record is a row of its own, named by path 1`] = `
"🐢 heres the wave...

🐚 git.pull.watch.get
   └─ daemon v<key> · live · pid <pid> · last tick <n>s ago
      ├─ home: <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=<key>/bin
      └─ watches
         ├─ ehmpathy/surf-demo#1220 → @:mechanic (<root:surf-demo>)
         └─ unreadable record: <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=<key>/watches/ehmpathy.surf-demo.pr=9.clone=c3.json

🥥 did you know?
   └─ a watch record that does not parse is held, never served, pick one
      ├─ read it: cat <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=<key>/watches/ehmpathy.surf-demo.pr=9.clone=c3.json
      └─ rewrite it from its clone: rhx git.pull.watch set --pr <n> --mode apply
"
`;

exports[`git.pull.watch faults given: [case5] a set while the daemon is paused when: [t0] the clone, already told of the pause, sets a second pr then: set names the pause on its own line 1`] = `
